    "content": "Empty directory — clean slate. To build the right thing, I have a few questions. Pick whatever fits; I'll fill in sensible defaults for anything you skip.\n\n**1. Platform / shape**\n- **Web app** (runs in browser, e.g. React + backend)?\n- **CLI tool** (manage bookmarks from the terminal)?\n- **Browser extension** (save the current tab with a click)?\n- Something else?\n\n**2. Scope — what should it actually do?** Common features:\n- Add/edit/delete bookmarks (URL, title, notes)\n- Tags and/or folders for organization\n- Search / filter\n- Auto-fetch page title & favicon when you paste a URL\n- Import/export (e.g. browser bookmarks, JSON)\n- Multi-user accounts, or just for you?\n\n**3. Storage & stack preferences**\n- Any language/framework you want (or want to avoid)?\n- Local-only (SQLite / a file) vs. a hosted database?\n\n**4. Aesthetics** — do you care about a polished UI, or is a functional MVP fine to start?\n\n---\n\nIf you'd rather I just **pick good defaults and start**, say the word and I'll scaffold a clean, local-first **web app** (React + TypeScript frontend, small Node/SQLite backend) with add/edit/delete, tags, and search — then we iterate from there.",
